                "source_case_id": "mediadive.ingredient:1030",
                "assessment": "CHEBI53437 expressly denotes nickel sulfate hexahydrate, with six-water formula and structure, CAS10101-97-0. The NiSO4 x6 owner already uses that identity but incorrectly stores anhydrous Ni.O4S/InChI/SMILES. A bounded proposal repairs those properties from the exact ontology. MediaDive1030 itself assigns anhydrous CAS7786-81-4 and molecular weight154.756 to the written hexahydrate; the source metadata remains contradictory. The separate Nickel_II_sulfate_hexahydrate owner and seven-water owner are not merged, and source/payload holds remain."
              },
              {
                "case_id": "KG_CASE:41c16262c44bcd5844262e5c7ee9ecb28dd0ff436ffc0ac3d1621a0278dae119",
                "source_case_id": "mediadive.ingredient:1634",
                "assessment": "CHEBI53504 explicitly specifies nickel(II):sulfate:water1:1:7 and CAS10101-98-1. The current seven-water owner identifier is appropriate but its InChI/SMILES still encode anhydrous salt. The bounded proposal corrects its structure/provenance from the exact ontology. MediaDive1634 retains anhydrous CAS7786-81-4 and mass despite the seven-water label, so this owner repair does not resolve source procurement or authorize cross-hydrate aliasing."
              }
            ]
