          "notes": "This is an ingredient/mixture has-part assertion, not an identity mapping, variant hierarchy, or complete culturing recipe. Successor dependency assessment: Moore 1976 confirms the historical Clostridium leptum PY-maltose use; its referenced manual formulation remains unread. The current exact-strain DSM 753 recipe has separate Trypticase peptone (BD BBL) and pepsin-digested meat peptone, 5 g each, and a maltose modification. This comparator demonstrates why neither ingredient may be chosen for the historical single peptone edge without a source bridge. No comparator quantities are imported. Withdraw the unsupported peptone component_id and set reference_scope UNMAPPED; retain its existing component_name as historical interpretation, not a newly observed expanded source label. The original assertion method and UNKNOWN/PARTIAL completeness remain unchanged. This is a bounded part-reference correction only. Whole-owner identity, raw labels, occurrence counts, quantities, unrelated components, all historical evidence and source/role/export holds are preserved. Historical all-components-identified statements describe prior states, not a new approval. No new MappingEvidence is added; historical human/component evidence enums are not rewritten."
