          "completeness": "UNKNOWN",
          "notes": "This is an ingredient/mixture has-part assertion, not an identity mapping, variant hierarchy, or complete culturing recipe. Current #1204/#204 correction: the source label supports literal rumen fluid, not clarified rumen fluid or a cow/JCM/DSMZ preparation. The processing claim and both the former MICRO0000520 link and proposed local clarified-fluid retarget are superseded. Preserve the named part as UNMAPPED without a component_id; no generic UBERON grounding or preparation guess is approved. Source-specific processing and whole-parent support remain withheld. Other parts, quantities, roles and completeness values are unchanged and not newly endorsed. https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1204#issuecomment-6718503591 Original part retained as historical provenance: {\"component_id\": \"MICRO:0000520\", \"component_name\": \"clarified rumen fluid\", \"reference_scope\": \"MIM_CATALOG\", \"source\": \"microbedecoder research decomposition (#213/#308)\"}\n\nCurrent source component assessment: This is an ingredient/mixture has-part assertion, not an identity mapping, variant hierarchy, or complete culturing recipe. The rumen-fluid component is retained at the literal source-label scope as rumen fluid, UNMAPPED, with no component identifier. The recovered MicrobeDecoder observation does not specify clarification, animal species, or a preparation protocol. The full cited publication was not retrieved in this review; the captured access failures cannot establish a protocol. This is unresolved processing, not evidence that the fluid was untreated. The former redirect to kgmicrobe.ingredient:clarified_rumen_fluid is withdrawn under https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1204#issuecomment-6718503591 and https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1237. Unrelated component identities, concentrations, whole-mixture identity and source holds are unchanged. Inherited mapping-evidence objects and research evidence remain historical provenance; their clarification claims and historical all-components-identified counts do not describe this successor. The prior 2026-11-08 dependency-only redirect event is preserved as superseded history. No generic UBERON grounding, recipe equivalence, animal-origin claim or downstream approval is added. Successor dependency assessment: The raw PYG + rumen fluid observation belongs to Eubacterium ruminantium. The original source chapter was inaccessible and the Bryant 1959 body access was challenge-blocked; the captured ATCC alternative medium listing is not a source recipe bridge. The original PYG base remains unresolved. Preserve the already corrected literal rumen-fluid UNMAPPED part and its processing/animal-origin holds. Withdraw the unsupported peptone component_id and set reference_scope UNMAPPED; retain its existing component_name as historical interpretation, not a newly observed expanded source label. The original assertion method and UNKNOWN/PARTIAL completeness remain unchanged. This is a bounded part-reference correction only. Whole-owner identity, raw labels, occurrence counts, quantities, unrelated components, all historical evidence and source/role/export holds are preserved. Historical all-components-identified statements describe prior states, not a new approval. No new MappingEvidence is added; historical human/component evidence enums are not rewritten."
