                "source_case_id": "mediadive.ingredient:628",
                "assessment": "The explicitly L-qualified source Na-L-malate has CAS138-09-0 and CHEBI91261, whose primary definition and structure are disodium (S)-malate. This source-specific L identity is compatible with the current owner. The owner also has explicitly DL aliases, independently contradicted by that stereospecific target; the bounded shared proposal rejects those racemate aliases but does not approve generic sodium-malate aliases or close the broader historical identity finding."
              },
              {
                "case_id": "KG_CASE:355c966549bfd528a2db00d73e618efa3f291ca3d1d0b34851800a4f43d9aa91",
                "source_case_id": "mediadive.ingredient:695",
                "assessment": "Na-DL-malate expressly denotes the racemic malate salt, whereas the attached CHEBI91261/CAS138-09-0 describe disodium (S)-malate. The source label and source identifiers conflict; the derived molarity does not settle stereochemistry. The exact owner proposal retains the text/source as REJECTED_LABEL on the L-specific owner, preventing a false resolving alias. It does not mint an unverified racemate record or close the broader Sodium_Malate identity finding."
              },
              {
                "case_id": "KG_CASE:6ff96a432d284768932c069b30ef2d0262cf5218e424f9783655dd94f9ec6a6d",
                "source_case_id": "mediadive.ingredient:204",
                "assessment": "Na2-DL-malate specifies both disodium stoichiometry and the DL racemate. CHEBI91261 is explicitly disodium (S)-malate, so its copied source CAS and current exact alias cannot override the stereochemical conflict. The shared proposal changes this and the other explicit DL names to non-resolving REJECTED_LABEL while preserving provenance; a new racemate identity remains unproven."
              },
              {
                "case_id": "KG_CASE:79232876ee0bf1e72b13d7468a47b59d8e0260447848d9b7a13d448f002c70e6",
                "source_case_id": "mediadive.ingredient:477",
                "assessment": "Na-malate carries no stereochemistry or sodium count in the source name, while ingredient477 assigns the L-specific CAS138-09-0/CHEBI91261. The same database assigns that target to explicit DL labels elsewhere, so its lookup alone is not independent stereochemical proof. Preserve the generic source token and existing owner as a candidate, without treating the name as a globally exact L alias. The shared DL-alias correction does not settle this generic entry."
              },
              {
                "case_id": "KG_CASE:91fbd30ef38331c306f684d5bc27b3b8da74ab0f203c2dd1839859d33421388c",
                "source_case_id": "mediadive.ingredient:1316",
                "assessment": "This source is25mL of filter-sterilized20% Na malate. It denotes an aqueous preparation with concentration and processing qualifiers, not identity with a neat malate salt. MediaDive1316 links L-specific CHEBI91261/CAS138-09-0, but the generic name alone does not establish stereochemistry, particularly given the same database L/DL conflicts. Keep stock context and the possible solute candidate separately; the shared DL-rejection proposal does not settle this stock."
              },
              {
                "case_id": "KG_CASE:c8c5f6d20657c12e8c7fa05a03c476097421221ae1970a15da8f48464dfd99c4",
                "source_case_id": "mediadive.ingredient:495",
                "assessment": "DL-Na-malate explicitly specifies racemic malate, but source495 and the current Sodium_Malate owner map it to disodium (S)-malate CHEBI91261/CAS138-09-0. The shared proposal preserves this exact source spelling as REJECTED_LABEL on that enantiomer-specific owner. Neither the copied CAS nor a molarity calculated with the salt mass eliminates the DL/L contradiction."
              }
